  {
   "id": "poole/MRK.2.13",
   "range": "MRK.2.13",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "7ded4167",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "poole/MRK.2.13#p1-7ded4167",
     "text": "Still it is said he taught them, thereby letting his ministers know what is their great work; and therefore they should be persons apt to teach, as Paul directeth Timothy, 1Ti 3:2.",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "1Ti 3:2",
       "ref": "1TI.3.2"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "poole/MRK.2.14",
   "range": "MRK.2.14",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "c767af87",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "poole/MRK.2.14#p1-c767af87",
     "text": "Ver. 14-17. We had this piece of history with some addition in Mat 9:9-13, where he was called Matthew: Mark and Luke both call him Levi: it was ordinary with the Jews to have two names. See Poole on \"Mat 9:9\".",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Mat 9:9-13",
       "ref": "MAT.9.9-13"
      },
      {
       "text": "Mat 9:9",
       "ref": "MAT.9.9"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
